# Scope the knowledge graph to work this repo actually owns.
#
# graphify walks the filesystem, and .gitignore does not cover git submodules
# (they are gitlinks, not ignored paths). Without these rules the graph fills
# up with vendored third-party code — Light Panda alone is a full browser
# engine — which buries the actual projects and makes every query noisier.

# --- vendored submodules --------------------------------------------------
# Upstream clones. Useful to have on disk, useless as graph nodes: we do not
# own this code and never answer questions about its internals.
External Repos/

# --- environments and installed packages ----------------------------------
Virtual Environments/
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/site-packages/

# --- reference material ---------------------------------------------------
# Textbooks and scanned PDFs. Large, and not code.
References/

# --- build output and local state -----------------------------------------
**/build/
**/dist/
**/.git/
graphify-out/
**/*.db
